    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement was: when an owner is created (and read back), return a `displayName` field formatted exactly as `'LastName, FirstName'` from the stored names.\n\nSince the response DTO (`OwnerDto`) is generated from the OpenAPI spec and serialized via MapStruct, I made two edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes it from the stored entity:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n           expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBecause both the create responder (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and the read responder (`RespondWithOwner`) route through `toOwnerDto`, the field appears consistently. The test creates an owner then reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` and asserts `$.displayName == \"LastName, John\"`.\n\n`AcceptanceTest` passes and `./mvnw test` reports **BUILD SUCCESS** with 0 failures/errors.",
